From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: a Unity game in Xbox controller mode gets the controller
 as a HID device

PW_RAWINPUT_PAD=2 for a Unity game (Wine patch 1046: an Xbox 360 controller's HID collection it can open), 1 for a Java game, which reads only raw input's list (#149).
---
 native/wine64_main.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/native/wine64_main.c b/native/wine64_main.c
index bae30b8..da8ad6e 100644
--- a/native/wine64_main.c
+++ b/native/wine64_main.c
@@ -1913,8 +1913,10 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
              * an XInput one through XInput: win32u lists the controller there
              * for a Unity game (patch 1033); other games see no change. */
             if (unity_game(prefix, game->app.executable)) {
-                extra[config.extra_env_count++] = (PwWineStartEnv){ "PW_RAWINPUT_PAD", "1" };
-                PS5LOG_LOG("PW_WINE64 raw input controller for a Unity game");
+                /* 2: a whole HID device (xinput1_3's dualsense.c as an Xbox 360 controller's
+                 * collection), which Unity's raw input opens before it reads XInput (#684). */
+                extra[config.extra_env_count++] = (PwWineStartEnv){ "PW_RAWINPUT_PAD", "2" };
+                PS5LOG_LOG("PW_WINE64 raw input controller for a Unity game: a HID device");
             } else if (java_game(prefix, game->app.executable)) {
                 /* so GLFW sees the XInput controller once (java_game) */
                 extra[config.extra_env_count++] = (PwWineStartEnv){ "PW_RAWINPUT_PAD", "1" };
